  "turning_point_description": "April 22, 2025. The Resistance Front (TRF) \u2014 an LeT proxy created in 2019 to provide FATF deniability \u2014 kills 26 tourists in the Baisaran Valley meadow near Pahalgam. 25 tourists (mostly Hindu) and one local Muslim pony operator are shot with M4 carbines and AK-47s. It is the deadliest civilian attack in India since 26/11. TRF initially claims responsibility twice, then retracts. ISI-TRF coordination is confirmed through signals intelligence. Rizwan Shah, now running operations from a position of deep knowledge of the ISI-LeT structure, must determine: was this an ISI-sanctioned escalation or a TRF operational overreach? The answer determines the appropriate scale and nature of India's response.",
  "real_world_correlation": {
    "event_date": "April 22, 2025",
    "real_event": "Pahalgam terrorist attack, Baisaran Valley, Anantnag district, J&K. 26 killed (25 tourists + 1 local). The Resistance Front (TRF) claimed responsibility twice (April 22-23) then denied. TRF is widely understood as an LeT-ISI proxy established post-Article 370 abrogation (October 2019) to maintain operational cover under FATF grey-listing scrutiny.",
    "trf_structure": "TRF was founded October 2019 after India's revocation of J&K's special status. It draws cadres from LeT and Hizbul Mujahideen. Its purpose is to allow ISI/LeT to claim plausible deniability for attacks while FATF scrutiny is active. Pakistan's nominal FATF compliance (grey list exit June 2022) did not end these operations.",
    "strategic_escalation": "The attack represents a strategic escalation from the previous pattern (security forces, political figures, infrastructure workers) to direct tourist targeting \u2014 a deliberate choice to damage Kashmir's tourism economy and signal India's inability to protect civilians. This type of target shift is consistent with ISI authorisation at a high level.",
    "india_response_timeline": "India's response escalated over two weeks: diplomatic (Indus Waters Treaty suspended, Pakistani diplomats expelled) and military (Operation Sindoor, May 7, 2025, striking 9 terror infrastructure targets in Pakistan and PoK)."
  },
